Z||000000||LoW_KeY||12-02-2001||04:43 PM||||Ok I'm not to hyped up about buying a kit sure I'm cheap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> but if it all comes down to it I will.. <P>anything else you can clean the filter with? simple green? just let it soak then dry? thanks.<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||2birds||12-02-2001||04:46 PM||||I'm a cheapo, too, but the kit is under $10 at most places, and it will last for 2-3 cleaning/re-oilings.  Still cheaper than a new OEM type filter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LoW_KeY||12-02-2001||05:09 PM||||Ahh ok didn't know you could use it that many times not to mention I thought it was like 30 bucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I feel dumb hehe..||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-02-2001||05:50 PM||||The cleaning stuff in the kit works really really good, you can see a lot of dirt that comes out.  You probably could use simple green, but I dont know if it has enough solvents to get rid of the filter oil.<P>And, anyways, you <B>do</B> need the oil, otherwise your filter will not trap as many particles with it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WampusCat||12-02-2001||05:55 PM||||I'd be worried that some other cleaner might shrink the cotton in the filter.  I always use the K&N stuff.  I'm a scaredy cat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LoW_KeY||12-02-2001||06:08 PM||||Hey Joe,<P>thanks, yeah I was wondering about the oil.. I took my filter out and its kinda dirty doesn't even look red I heard somewhere you could use Simple Green, but again I'd be stumped on the oil.. I'll have to go out and buy the kit when I get a cash flow comin' in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||12-03-2001||01:04 AM||||Just toss the filter in the dishwasher, then re-oil after it comes out.  I've even heard of Ferrari Cup mechanics doing it this way.  That's how I do it on my K&N.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jefrysuko||12-03-2001||01:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Just toss the filter in the dishwasher, then re-oil after it comes out.  I've even heard of Ferrari Cup mechanics doing it this way.  That's how I do it on my K&N.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have a few friends that do this also.  One of them even has a dishwasher installed in his garage to clean parts with.  It really does a good job and dosn't destroy the filter just don't use the dry cycle or let the wife know.||||reg||1
Z||000008||maryjane||12-03-2001||01:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jefrysuko:<BR><B> I have a few friends that do this also.  One of them even has a dishwasher installed in his garage to clean parts with.  It really does a good job and dosn't destroy the filter just don't use the dry cycle or let the wife know.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I heard that! I let Jane catch me using the oven to expand a flywheel ring gear, now I have to do all the cooking. As far as she knows, the dishwasher and all the other appliances are far above my operational skills. I hate laundry and dishwashing!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||12-03-2001||02:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR>I heard that! I let Jane catch me using the oven to expand a flywheel ring gear, now I have to do all the cooking. As far as she knows, the dishwasher and all the other appliances are far above my operational skills. I hate laundry and dishwashing!<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, you're doing it all wrong dude!  Dishes and laundry are the EASY ones, especially with modern appliances, you don't hardly have to do anything.<P>The duties you are supposed to weasel out of are things like dusting, vacuumming, mopping, and all other tedious jobs.  especially dusting, I hate dusting!  I say if you use it or put something on it so rarely that dust develops, it doesn't need to be dusted anyway!  Unfortunately, females don't think that way <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dumba$$||12-03-2001||08:47 AM||||i just spray it with simple green and then throw it in the dishwasher||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||12-03-2001||10:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jefrysuko:<BR><B> just don't use the dry cycle or let the wife know.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>VERY valid points!  Definately DON'T use the dry cycle!!!  You're on your own with the wife, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I also typically run my diswasher again empty after cleaning the filter - just in case - to wash out anything that my be lingering.  I've never noticed any problem with anything getting on dishes etc.  You do have to be careful using the oven for car stuff, though.  It can alter the flavor of the foods, if you're not careful (depending on what you're doing).<P>I want to get a spare electric oven for the garage so I can do my own powder coating at home!  Of course, I need the garage first.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000012||webbee||12-03-2001||11:16 AM||||If you want to avoid trouble with the wife, mix up dish washer detergent and hot water in a bucket and let it soak for an hour. Rinse it off and let it air dry. The mixture is reusable.||||reg||1
Z||000013||NEPTUNE||12-03-2001||04:43 PM||||I use 409 or Fantastic, with a nozzle on the garden hose to clean it, then oil it with atf. No problems so far.||||reg||3
Z||000014||rogergarrison||12-03-2001||05:27 PM||||I got the cleaner. after 2 hours trying to get the crap out, is said the hell with it and bought a new one, $25 wasnt worth the trouble. anyone want a used K&N with cleaner/oil kit?...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||cadaver||12-03-2001||08:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NEPTUNE:<BR><B>I use 409 or Fantastic, with a nozzle on the garden hose to clean it, then oil it with atf. No problems so far.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>NO NO NO<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Nashco||12-03-2001||08:56 PM||||I'm all for saving a buck if you can get the same results...but seriously people.  There are some things that you just don't do, it's common sense.  The K&N isn't your standard cotton/paper filter.  Using anything harsh will damage it, and using the incorrect oil will hamper it.  Yeah, you may be able to use dish detergent...as a base cleaning.  What about doing it first with mild dish soap and hand rinsing, THEN using the proper cleaners?  It's ok to avoid using too much, but not using the specified oil on your K&N is just like using the wrong fluid in your accessories.<P>Would you use brake fluid in your transmission, just because you didn't notice anything bad happen?  How about putting some comet and water in your wiper squirter?  I'm sure you can do them without seeing any major problems...at first.<P>Well, I made my recommendation, for what it's worth.  FYI, my K&N experience has been in major abuse environments.  I use one on my baja VW in the sand dunes.  Using K&N oil it trapped about twice as much particles as any other method, about four times as much as it did without any oil at all.  I used mild soap and water to get the first couple runs of grit out, but the K&N cleaner always got a little more out of it with one more clean.  Another application of K&N oil and a good bake in the sun for a while and my car was ready to go.  I used the same cleaning kit about 10 times with success.<P>Come on guys, there are some things you can be cheap on.  Be cheap on which cookies you buy, or which phone company to use, but don't be so cheap you won't treat your "performance filter" to a 1.15 lunch.<P>&lt;/RANT&gt;<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000017||webbee||12-03-2001||10:06 PM||||When I first purchased K&N filters there was no cleaning kit. The distributor I bought them from told me to only use automatic dishwasher soap, mixed with warm water, soak for an hour, then air dry. I was also told to only use K&N oil sparingly. 1 drop per pleat. I just replaced my original K&N's after about 14 years of service on a VW van. I followed the above procedure about every 6k miles. They were still good, showing no holes in any of the pleats. So I must be doing something right. <BR>I think that you should buy 2 filters & alternate them. Makes clean up & replacement much simpler. You probably would never have to replace them again. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Standard||12-04-2001||03:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Would you use brake fluid in your transmission, just because you didn't notice anything bad happen?  How about putting some comet and water in your wiper squirter?  I'm sure you can do them without seeing any major problems...at first.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think a better example here would be... Would you use ATF in your clutch hydraulics?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000019||LoW_KeY||12-04-2001||10:46 PM||||Wow I took the words from ya guys and bought one..<P>I must say a lot of crap came out of that! I have my air intake a little different its outside the canistor, my friend seems to think thats why it got so dirty, but its been on the car for some time.<P>Anyways while cleaning it I got it almost white looking then oiled her down.  The filter was pretty much black, I'm a bit curious how much better it'll breathe now.  I know from past experiences having a crappy filter really shot down my performance.<P>thanks a bunch! <P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by LoW_KeY (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
